==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cutie MOMOCO''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Starlight MOMOCO''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Wonder MOMOCO is an amazing crowd-control unit for Red, Dark, and Angels, who also performs greatly in many stages. The first part of her attack sends out a massive [[Wave Attack]], clearing out any lesser peons so your other units can advance toward the main threats. This first attack also [[Freeze|Freezes]] Red, Dark, and Angel enemies for 2 seconds (not accounting for [[Fruit Treasures]]), giving your shorter-ranged cats an opportunity to get their hits in. She also has fine health and is immune to wave attacks.

The second hit isn't anything special, but the third and final hit is surprisingly strong. While she may seem like just a support unit at first glance, MOMOCO has an astonishing 9,132 DPS. The final attack in her [[Multi-Hit]] can deal heavy blows to the remaining enemies that weren't knocked back or killed entirely by the Wave Attack from her first two hits.

The main drawbacks that MOMOCO has are her low overall stamina, caused by mediocre range and a low amount of knockbacks. She also may has a huge tendency to whiff her final attack. All these traits combined make MOMOCO an incredibly well-rounded unit with high damage and excellent crowd control capabilities.

==='''True Form'''===
To start, Starlight MOMOCO has her Freeze's duration improved by 1 second, bringing the ability's uptime to a whopping 53%, which is a ''wonder''ful upgrade on a unit with such wide effective reach and expansive coverage in targets. This alone makes the True Form worth getting, but she's also fitted with much better survivability (+30% HP) and more rewarding damage on her final Multi-Hit (+~29%). Her DPS is still very difficult to consistently employ in the heat of battle, so this change should be considered a bonus for tankier enemies like [[Berserkory]] and [[Boraphim]], who are easier to keep still until she finishes her foreswing animation. Regardless, keeping her alive is much less of a hassle now, and she keeps herself much healthier against targets, since they can't exactly retaliate if they're Frozen.

[[Colossus Slayer]] is alright. It improves MOMOCO's performance in three [[Gauntlet|Colossus Gauntlets]]: [[Baron Seal Strikes]], [[Divine Archangel Strikes]], and the second half of [[Horrorpotamus]] despite not targeting the boss. She already naturally outranges all three Colossus bosses, so what this ability does is primarily complement her DPS against them. All three of them are hyper-aggressive pushers; nothing survives being in their effective range, so this ability does nothing to improve her survivability against them—outside of [[Archangel Exiel]]—especially when she only has one opportunity to reposition. Instead, it makes her final hit deal a mini-nuke of 95,200 damage at Lv.30, or 151,200 at Lv.50. Considering her attack rate, it's not bad damage at all, and most of the Colossus bosses are bulky enough to hold still until this ''cutie'' is able to finish her attack cycle. The stages in question all heavily favor her usage as well, with [[Horrorpotamus/Cosmic Juggernaut Lv.1~20|Cosmic Juggernaut Lv.11~20]] in particular featuring [[Tackey]] as a problematic annoyance that you can reliably Freeze. Outside of these Gauntlets, the ability gives her great additional tankiness when throwing hands with [[Great Angel Chibinel]] and [[J.J. Jackrabbit]] in particular, however infrequent their appearances may be.

Starlight MOMOCO's immunities are fine enough in applicability. While the aforementioned damage buff isn't the easiest to fully utilize, [[Immune to Weaken]] theoretically helps her maintain it against [[Dark Dober]], [[Puffzerker]], and [[Winged Pigge]], all of which cut DPS to a meager 10-25%. However, outranging said enemies is usually good enough to avoid the debuff entirely, which means in practice, it doesn't really do much. It can definitely help whenever she's hit by high-range Weakeners like Great Angel Chibinel and [[Calamary]], so it's not entirely useless. [[Immune to Freeze]] is a counter to [[Henry]]. It allows her to get consistent hits off in direct confrontations with [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]] and [[CTO Seal]] too, but tanking damage isn't her forte, and she is likely to get quickly shredded by the former. All of this, coupled with the price drop from ¢4,500 -> ¢3,750, makes this a great True Form all-around.

