==Trivia==
*Wonder MOMOCO heavily references the arcade game ''[[wikipedia:Wonder Momo|Wonder Momo]]'', which centers on an actress playing the role of a "wonder girl", a galactic superheroine that fights the villainous Warudemon army while wearing a similar dress to MOMOCO.
**In the 2012 ShiftyLook webcomic and the 2014 anime mini-series, Wonder Momo has a daughter who goes by Momoko, which is the same as MOMOCO's romanized Japanese name.
**Aside from kicking her enemies, Wonder Momo is able to fire [[Wave Attack|wave attacks]], just like Wonder MOMOCO.
**Wonder MOMOCO's Japanese description mentions that she eliminates "warumono", which would normally mean "bad guys". However, the description has it written in katakana (ワルモノ), which could be a reference to Warudemon (ワルデモン).
*Wonder MOMOCO may also be a reference to [[wikia:keroro:Poyon|Poyon]] from ''[[wikipedia:Sgt. Frog|Sgt. Frog]]''. Both are cosmic policewomen who wield similar-looking blasters, the skirt of Wonder MOMOCO's dress looks almost identical to Poyon's, and her Evolved Form wears an antenna hairband.
*Judging by her Evolved Form's character portrait in the [[Upgrade Menu]], the flying saucers apparently should have had a different appearance than her Normal Form, it shows a more rounded saucer with a heart stamp instead of a star one, with a striped pattern instead of a plain texture.
*Wonder MOMOCO was featured alongside the original nine [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] in a special challenge version of the [[Empire of Cats]] stage [[Alaska (Empire of Cats)|Hokkaido Prefecture]] that could be played in the shopping mall booths that were set up to commemorate [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]]'s [[Anniversary/7th Year|7th anniversary]].
*Wonder MOMOCO, [[Emperor Cat (Legend Rare Cat)|Emperor Cat]] and [[Legeluga (Legend Rare Cat)|Legeluga]] are the only [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cats]] to not have the Insane Damage or Insanely Tough abilities.

